{"id":"girls-names","title":"Most common girls' names in the US","prompt":"Name the 10 most common names for baby girls born in the US from 1926 to 2025","noun":"girls' names","category":"Oddball","metric":"Rank, 1926-2025 (Social Security records)","lowerIsBetter":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: Popularity of birth names for females (United States)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popularity_of_birth_names_for_females_(United_States)","asOf":"2026-11-02","dataAsOf":"2025"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"Mary","aliases":[],"value":"#1","n":1,"article":"Mary (name)","fact":{"text":"St. Jerome translated it as \"drop of the sea\"; a scribal error turned that into \"star of the sea\", Stella Maris.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_(name)"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Patricia","aliases":[],"value":"#2","n":2,"article":"Patricia","fact":{"text":"It peaked at third for newborn girls from 1937 to 1943; by 2016 it had slid to 745th.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patricia"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Jennifer","aliases":[],"value":"#3","n":3,"article":"Jennifer (given name)","fact":{"text":"It's the Cornish form of Guinevere, and was rare elsewhere until George Bernard Shaw used it in The Doctor's Dilemma.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jennifer_(given_name)"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Linda","aliases":[],"value":"#4","n":4,"article":"Linda (given name)","fact":{"text":"The 1946 song \"Linda\" was named after the songwriter's lawyer's one-year-old daughter: the future Linda McCartney.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linda_(1946_song)"}},{"rank":5,"name":"Elizabeth","aliases":[],"value":"#5","n":5,"article":"Elizabeth (given name)","fact":{"text":"It comes from the Hebrew Elisheva, \"My God is an oath\", the name of Aaron's wife in the Bible.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_(given_name)"}},{"rank":6,"name":"Barbara","aliases":[],"value":"#6","n":6,"article":"Barbara (given name)","fact":{"text":"It's from the Greek for \"foreign\", 